co.uk/documents/s29076/appendix-f-treasury-management-strategy.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"12/02/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Human Resources Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-07","committee":"Planning Policy Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-05","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Cabinet","time":"3.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-26","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-03","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-10","committee":"Cabinet","time":"3.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Cabinet","time":"3.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Council consciously elected to invest asset sale proceeds in deposits rather than reduce \u00a3115 million in PWLB debt.","lead":"This shows the council chose to maintain debt levels despite having proceeds available, reflecting deliberate capital strategy and priorities. The council is paying \u00a32.718 million annually in borrowing costs while generating \u00a31.666 million in deposit\u2026","iso":"2026-07-09","paper_title":"EHDC 2526 Treasury Management Report Final","paper_url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30311/30311.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Council disposed of investment portfolio assets to replace income now lost, generating \u00a31.666 million from temporary deposits instead.","lead":"A lender would want to know the council has lost a revenue stream, forcing a shift to temporary deposits rather than permanent income sources. These deposits will mature between April and December 2026, creating a question about income continuity.","iso":"2026-07-09","paper_title":"EHDC 2526 Treasury Management Report Final","paper_url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30311/30311.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Rising homelessness with explicit warnings of sustained future increases due to Renters Rights Act implementation","lead":"Anticipated sustained increases in homelessness could create significant budget pressures, particularly for temporary accommodation costs and officer time if the council cannot contain demand.","iso":"2026-07-09","paper_title":"Appendix A EHDC Quarterly Performance Report Q4","paper_url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30304/30304.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-09","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"EHDC 2526 Treasury Management Report Final","paper_url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30311/30311.pdf","headline":"Council consciously elected to invest asset sale proceeds in deposits rather than reduce \u00a3115 million in PWLB debt.","detail":"The capital receipts from asset disposals were explicitly ringfenced for Treasury Management deposits instead of debt repayment. No new PWLB loans were taken in 2025/26, but the council's external borrowing remains \u00a3115.093 million, with only scheduled repayments of \u00a32.008 million made.","category":"borrowing","matters":"This shows the council chose to maintain debt levels despite having proceeds available, reflecting deliberate capital strategy and priorities. The council is paying \u00a32.718 million annually in borrowing costs while generating \u00a31.666 million in deposit returns\u2014a net negative carry position.","figures":"\u00a3115.093 million external borrowing; \u00a32.718 million borrowing costs; \u00a31.666 million deposit income; \u00a345 million in new deposits","quote":"Per the roadmap, the capital receipts were ringfenced for investing in Treasury Management and not to repay the PWLB loans.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-09","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"EHDC 2526 Treasury Management Report Final","paper_url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30311/30311.pdf","headline":"Council disposed of investment portfolio assets to replace income now lost, generating \u00a31.666 million from temporary deposits instead.","detail":"The council sold investment and operational assets during 2025/26, deploying approximately \u00a345 million in new deposits to generate treasury income. The paper explicitly states this new income stream is required because the council's existing Investment Portfolio income has reduced. This is a deliberate strategic shift following a property roadmap.","category":"income","matters":"A lender would want to know the council has lost a revenue stream, forcing a shift to temporary deposits rather than permanent income sources. These deposits will mature between April and December 2026, creating a question about income continuity.","figures":"\u00a345 million increase in deposits from 2024/25 to 2025/26; \u00a31.666 million generated in 2025/26; deposits maturing at various dates through December 2026","quote":"The Treasury Management interest generated from the deposits is required to replace the reduced income from the Investment Portfolio.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-09","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A EHDC Quarterly Performance Report Q4","paper_url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30304/30304.pdf","headline":"Rising homelessness with explicit warnings of sustained future increases due to Renters Rights Act implementation","detail":"Homelessness approaches have risen this quarter, particularly due to landlords serving notice before the Renters Rights Act takes effect. The council warns: 'Longer term this may result in a reduction of private rented units available within the district, which is likely to further increase homelessness approaches' and that supporting these cases will 'lead to more officer time and much longer cases, as court delay for defending possession proceedings are expected.' Households in temporary B&B accommodation rose from 17 at start of year to 30 by end of Q4.","category":"demand","matters":"Anticipated sustained increases in homelessness could create significant budget pressures, particularly for temporary accommodation costs and officer time if the council cannot contain demand.","figures":"Households in B&B: 30 at end Q4 (up from 17 at start of year); homelessness acceptances Q1-Q4: 0, 7, 13, 8","quote":"Longer term this may result in a reduction of private rented units available within the district, which is likely to further increase homelessness approaches. Supporting future homelessness approaches from private rented accommodation will also lead to more officer time and much longer cases, as court delay for defending possession proceedings are expected.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-09","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A EHDC Quarterly Performance Report Q4","paper_url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30304/30304.pdf","headline":"Corporate Services budget overspend of \u00a30.382m with no explanation provided in the report","detail":"Corporate Services had a budget of \u00a35.764m with an outturn of \u00a36.145m, resulting in a \u00a30.382m (6.6%) overspend. This variance is not explained in the narrative sections. Corporate Services includes Legal, Democratic Services, Elections, HR, IT, and Communications. The unexplained nature of the overspend raises questions about budget control.","category":"governance","matters":"Material departmental overspends without explanation could indicate budget control weaknesses or hidden cost pressures that might recur.","figures":"Budget: \u00a35.764 million, Outturn: \u00a36.145 million, Variance: \u00a30.382 million","quote":"Budget: \u00a35.764 million\nOutturn: \u00a36.145 million\nVariance: \u00a30.382 million","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-09","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"EHDC 2526 Outturn Report","paper_url":"https://easthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30308/30308.pdf","headline":"Investment property portfolio incurring \u00a30.400m in legal and holding costs on a surplus asset","detail":"The council drew \u00a30.400m from reserves for legal and holding costs on an investment property, suggesting the asset is not generating expected returns or is otherwise underutilised. No detail is given on the property, its acquisition cost, or recovery timeline.","category":"other","matters":"Property holdings that generate costs rather than revenue indicate either poor asset management decisions or market conditions affecting expected returns, both of which are material for a lender assessing council financial resilience.","figures":"\u00a30.400 million drawdown for investment property legal and holding costs","quote":"There was also a drawdown relating to the costs associated with our Investment Portfolio whereby we have incurred legal and holding costs (\u00a30.400 million).","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-23"},"name":"East Hampshire","findings_total":25,"news_drafts_total":3}}